Korea Legal Index
=================

Data source
-----------
This software reads Korean statutory law through the official open data API of
the National Law Information Center (국가법령정보, 법제처), served at
law.go.kr and open.law.go.kr.

This repository bundles no legal text. The software fetches it live at run time.
The MIT license covers only this software, not the legal data.

Reuse terms of the data (verified at the official source on 2026-10-24,
https://www.law.go.kr/lawPetitionForm.do?menuId=13&subMenuId=79):
- Korean statutes and court decisions (법령, 판례, etc.) are works not protected
  by copyright under Copyright Act Article 7 (저작권법 제7조). You may use them
  freely, with no separate permission.
- The Public Data Act (공공데이터의 제공 및 이용 활성화에 관한 법률) guarantees
  free use of this legal information, commercial use included.
- The center states that it actively supports individuals and organizations that
  link (연계) the legal information into their own services.

Conditions you must still honor:
- Do not alter or forge the legal text, and do not present altered text as
  authoritative. Preserve the verbatim text and link to the official source.
- Do not harm the center's service (for example, through excessive request
  volume). Use the API within its rate limits and in good faith.
- Do not include data that carries third-party rights or non-disclosure
  restrictions.

Attribution
-----------
Attribution is good practice, not a copyright condition for non-protected works.
When you display legal text obtained through this software, name the source as
국가법령정보센터 (National Law Information Center) and link to the official
source URL that each record carries.

Not legal advice
